CIVIL 3D MCP EDIT AND SEWERGEMS FIXES
====================================
Date 2026-11-21
Release 0.10.0

Scope
-----
This change log covers the three issues selected for the first fix pass.
It records drawing targeting, edit retries, and SewerGEMS import behavior.
Paths are relative to the project folder.

01  plugin/Core/DrawingTarget.cs
--------------------------------
Added
  - Per-document UUIDs, bridge session identity, target parsing, and active
    drawing validation.
Removed
  - None.
Modified
  - New file.
Why
  - Bind a write to the same open drawing across tab switches and distinguish a
    reopened DWG.

02  plugin/Bridge/BridgeServer.cs
---------------------------------
Added
  - Session IDs in bridge discovery and drawing targets in read responses.
Removed
  - The path that sent all actions through the same UI dispatch without checking
    a target.
Modified
  - Routes edits through the request tracker and serves get_edit_status
    independently of the Civil 3D UI queue.
Why
  - Detect a changed bridge instance and allow status checks while an edit is
    waiting or running.

03  plugin/Bridge/EditRequests.cs
---------------------------------
Added
  - Thread-safe tracking of pending, completed, and error states, payload
    fingerprints, and bounded caching of recent replies.
Removed
  - None.
Modified
  - New file.
Why
  - Prevent the same request ID from running twice and retain its outcome for
    safe retry.

04  plugin/Core/Registry.cs
---------------------------
Added
  - Registered get_edit_status as a read action.
Removed
  - None.
Modified
  - The registry exposes 41 read actions.
Why
  - Make edit outcomes discoverable through both desktop clients.

05  plugin/Core/WriteGate.cs
----------------------------
Added
  - Approval and refusal timestamps stored per open drawing.
Removed
  - The session-wide approval and cooldown fields.
Modified
  - Updated approval, revocation, audit messages, and the late-answer behavior.
Why
  - Granting access to one drawing should not grant access to other open
    drawings.

06  plugin/Plugin.cs
--------------------
Added
  - None.
Removed
  - Session-wide wording for MCPALLOW.
Modified
  - MCPALLOW now grants permission for the active drawing.
Why
  - Make the command match the scope of the edit permission check.

07  plugin/Edit/EditEngine.cs
-----------------------------
Added
  - Target checks before permission, after permission, under the document lock,
    and before deferred file actions.
Removed
  - The old check that only detected a change during the permission dialog.
Modified
  - Records request UUIDs in edit audits and reports deferred file-action
    problems as warnings after commit.
Why
  - Keep edits and file actions bound to the requested drawing and give retries
    a traceable result.

08  plugin/Edit/EditContext.cs
------------------------------
Added
  - A set of resolved object IDs used to deduplicate handles per operation.
Removed
  - Repeated processing of the same object when a handle was supplied twice.
Modified
  - Resolves the Civil 3D document from the locked database.
Why
  - Ensure an object moves or copies once per operation, even when handles are
    repeated.

09  plugin/Read/DrawingRead.cs
------------------------------
Added
  - The Civil 3D drawing unit value in get_drawing_info.
Removed
  - None.
Modified
  - Drawing info reports drawing units as well as AutoCAD insertion units.
Why
  - Allow the importer to verify the drawing uses metres before using metric
    elevations and coordinates.

10  plugin/Edit/GravityOps.cs
-----------------------------
Added
  - Named pipe endpoints, connection verification, and optional metric bore and
    invert verification.
Removed
  - Automatic selection of the first candidate when several structures fell
    inside the tolerance.
Modified
  - Indexes structures by name and reports ambiguous geometric connections.
Why
  - Preserve the intended network topology and reject a pipe that Civil 3D
    cannot place at the requested levels.

11  plugin/Edit/AlignmentOps.cs
-------------------------------
Added
  - Optional filters for gravity pipe and structure names when adding parts to a
    profile view.
Removed
  - Repeated profile attachment attempts for the same resolved object.
Modified
  - Uses named parts from the newly created network within the import
    transaction.
Why
  - Build each profile with its own parts before committing the core import.

12  plugin/Edit/DrawOps.cs
--------------------------
Added
  - The draw_annotations operation for grouped line, text, and multiline-text
    items.
Removed
  - None.
Modified
  - The edit registry exposes 69 operations.
Why
  - Keep a band table with hundreds of annotations within the 500-operation edit
    batch limit.

13  server/bridge_client.py
---------------------------
Added
  - UUID and target validation, selected-session matching, and a fresh request
    UUID on get_drawing_info.
Removed
  - The generic timeout advice to check a permission prompt before resending.
Modified
  - Verifies reply IDs, closes the reply stream explicitly, and points
    interrupted writes to get_edit_status.
Why
  - Fail safely with an old or different add-in and let the caller recover the
    original outcome.

14  server/server.py
--------------------
Added
  - Required target and request ID inputs on the split edit tool.
Removed
  - The split edit call that accepted operations without a drawing target.
Modified
  - Passes the target and request ID through the existing edit dispatcher.
Why
  - Apply the same drawing and retry rules to standard and split tool modes.

15  server/sewergems.py
-----------------------
Added
  - Flow validation, metric checks, unique branch names, strict catalogue
    matching, explicit endpoints, and separate finish attempt IDs.
Removed
  - Recursive upstream traversal, catalogue downsizing fallback, and unreported
    failures in later import batches.
Modified
  - Uses one core transaction for network, profiles, and styles. Groups view
    placement and bands in a recorded finishing transaction.
Why
  - Reject malformed networks before writing and recover finishing without
    rebuilding a committed network.

16  server/catalog.py
---------------------
Added
  - Documentation for required target and request IDs, status lookup, named
    endpoints, grouped annotations, and finish_attempt.
Removed
  - The description of approval for every drawing in the session and the
    network-only import dry run.
Modified
  - Updates the standard and split tool descriptions and SewerGEMS options.
Why
  - Tell the MCP client how to prepare a safe edit and recover a result after an
    interruption.

17  plugin/BridgeInfo.cs
------------------------
Added
  - None.
Removed
  - Version 0.9.0 from the new build.
Modified
  - Set the bridge version to 0.10.0.
Why
  - Identify the build with the new write request contract.

18  plugin/PackageContents.xml
------------------------------
Added
  - None.
Removed
  - The previous bundle version and permission description from the new
    manifest.
Modified
  - Set the version to 0.10.0 and describe drawing-scoped approval.
Why
  - Keep the Autodesk bundle identifier and build version in sync.

19  README.md
-------------
Added
  - Instructions for drawing targets, request status, metric imports, and
    finishing retries.
Removed
  - The session-wide edit approval description and unconditional atomicity
    claims.
Modified
  - Updated version, tool counts, examples, command behavior, and import stages.
Why
  - Explain the current edit contract and the boundary between drawing
    transactions and deferred file operations.

20  package/INSTALL.txt
-----------------------
Added
  - None.
Removed
  - The approval description that applied to every drawing in a session.
Modified
  - Updated the quick guide to describe per-drawing approval.
Why
  - Keep the packaged setup guide consistent with Civil 3D.

